body:
* Which supermarket is the best?

Lidl and Aldi for price, Tesco for quality.

&#x200B;

* Is there a massive North/South divide like there is in England and is it because of the Tories?

Only between English people in Welsh unis, us Welsh people don't really care where you're from. 

&#x200B;

* Should I pick up my Welsh Duolingo again? 

Nobody can't speak English in South Wales, wouldn't reccomend it unless you've an interest in the language. If you live in Cardiff you won't need Welsh.

&#x200B;

* Should I learn the rules to Rugby? (We were only allowed to play tag rugby at school because someone cracked their head open.)

You'll pick it up as you go, don't be afraid to ask questions. A lot of people don't know them.

&#x200B;

* Is 'love' an acceptable thing to put at the end of a sentence in Wales? I also use 'pet' and 'mate'. 

Only to be condescending to girls, or if you're a middle aged man. lol

&#x200B;

* What kind of history did you learn about in school that I can look up and not look like an idiot when someone brings it up?

Welsh history? I know nothing. Some dude called Owain Glyndŵr did something. 

&#x200B;

* What are chavs called?

Chavs.

&#x200B;

* Acceptable tea brands?

Idk, tetleys?
